    {
      "rid": "doc_1.src_content.1",
      "doc": "doc_1",
      "category": "src_content",
      "full_page": "\"False humility trouble & the sadness we feel at sight of our sins are among the most subtle of the devil's snares,\" Humility & sorrow which comes from God, consoles and pacifies the soul. St. Teresa \"One of the best means to continue in the prac- tice of those good purposes we make in prayer is that we recolect the reason which had in- fluenced us to form them; because that which ocasioned the 1st thought will afterwards help us to conserve & practice it.\" St. Austin \"O Lord, if Thou art pleased to bestow thy gifts upon me be thou the guardian thereof thyself, for I have a diffidence in myself and I am a great robber who may prove bankrupt to Thee.\" St. Francis \"God chose a life of suffering. - The Way the Truth & the Life.\"",
